WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:01.500
Arby’s.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:03.120
R. B.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.670
Roast beef.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.150
That sounds like
a mystery solved.

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:08.995
Except those
letters stand for

00:00:09.035 --> 00:00:10.170
something else.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:12.834
But according to
Arby’s parent company,

00:00:12.874 --> 00:00:15.388
the name refers to
the Raffel Brothers:

00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:16.950
Leroy and Forrest.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:20.343
They founded the
restaurant in Boardman,

00:00:20.383 --> 00:00:21.810
Ohio, in 1964.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.560
Raffel Brothers.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:25.180
R. B.

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.530
Arby’s.

00:00:26.770 --> 00:00:29.927
The initials belong to
the founders. The roast

00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:32.198
beef makes the
coincidence especially

00:00:32.238 --> 00:00:33.570
easy to believe.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.020
Now you know.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.110
Ordinary has secrets.
